"products\ndocs\nblog\ncontact\nget_started\nRius is an Arize alternative built for companies shipping agents every day.\n\nPhoenix means running your own stack. AX includes 25k–50k spans a month. Rius is managed, real-time and includes 500k spans for $19/mo.\n\ntry 1 month free\n→\ntalk to the founders\n\n1 month free, then $19/mo · managed · 500k spans included\n\ninstrument your agent in 2 minutes ↓\nSilent failure detection\nMCP Observability\nLive spans\nAgent heartbeats\nUsed by:\nBacked by CEOs of:\n\n\"Rius found agent failures we didn't know existed. Our time to debug went from days to minutes and now we catch issues before they ever reach a customer.\"\n\nAndres Almansa\nCEO of Restack\n\nRius vs Arize AX\nvs Arize AX\nvs Phoenix OSS\n\tRius\tArize AX Free / Pro\n\n01\nDetection:\n\tReal-time, unlimited. Loops, context overflow, error patterns.\tSignal scans every 3–6 h. 10 / 25 issues/mo.\n\n02\nRoot cause:\n\tAutomatic per incident. Step, tool, change.\tPattern summary + fix idea. Alyx chat on request.\n\n03\nHeartbeat:\n\tPer span. Frozen agent = incident in seconds.\t“No data” per time window, not per run.\n\n04\nAlerts:\n\tUnlimited, to Slack and agents over MCP.\tMetric-threshold monitors → Slack, PagerDuty.\n\n05\nMCP:\n\tMCP-first. Incidents, RCAs, traces, alerts.\tNot documented (CLI + Skills).\n\n06\nUser view:\n\tPer end user: traces, failures, cost.\tFilter by user.id.\n\n07\nLimits:\n\t500k spans · 60 days\t25k / 50k spans · 15 / 30 days\n\n08\nPrice:\n\t$19/mo, managed. First month free.\t$0 / $50 per month. SaaS.\nWhere Arize stops.\n\nStrong for evals and experiments. These are the gaps in production.\n\nScheduled, not real-time\n\nSignal reviews traces every 3–6 hours.\n\nA loop at 9:02 shows up after the next scan\nAlyx investigates only when you ask\nNo per-run heartbeat for frozen agents\nLow limits\n\nFree and Pro run out fast with agents.\n\n25k / 50k spans per month\n15 / 30 days retention\n10 / 25 Signal issues per month\nPhoenix in production\n\nFree to download. Not free to run.\n\nPostgreSQL, backups, auth, upgrades\nOne tenant per instance\nNo built-in alerting\nSome of the silent failures that Rius would have caught for you.\nINFRASTRUCTURE\n\nTrace is green but one span shows an error\n\nThe run reports success. One tool call inside it failed and the agent carried on with bad data. Rius flags the span, not just the run.\n\nCOGNITIVE\n\nTool loop\n\nThe agent calls the same tool with near-identical arguments again and again. Every call returns 200. Rius flags the loop.\n\nINFRASTRUCTURE\n\nConsistent error pattern\n\nThe same failure signature across many runs, like a deprecated model name in config. Rius groups it into one incident with counts.\n\nINFRASTRUCTURE\n\nThe process that vanished\n\nNo output, no error, no end. The heartbeat stops and Rius opens an incident within seconds.\n\nRECOVERY\n\nThe run that crashed\n\nThe agent died mid-run. Rius keeps every span sent before the crash, so you see exactly where it stopped.\n\nCOGNITIVE\n\nThe wrong turn at step 7\n\nThe agent diverged early and kept going for 180 more steps. Rius shows the first divergence, not just the wrong final answer.\n\nInstrument your agent in 2 minutes.\n\nNo servers, no collector, no database. Paste one prompt into your coding agent and it wires up the Rius SDK for you.\n\nPYTHON\nTYPESCRIPT\nINSTALL PROMPT\nCOPY\nInstrument this code with the Rius SDK:\n\n# install the extra for the LLM library the code uses; it auto-instruments it:\npip install \"glassflow-rius[openai]\"   # or [anthropic], [langchain], ...; [instruments] for all\n\nimport rius\nrius.init(service_name=\"my-agent\")     # reads the API key from RIUS_API_KEY\n\nProvide the key as the RIUS_API_KEY environment variable (or in an env file). Never hardcode it.\nDocs: https://docs.glassflow.ai/rius/sdk\n01\nSign up and copy your API key.\n02\nPaste the prompt into Claude Code, Cursor or any coding agent.\n03\nRun your agent. Traces and incidents show up in Rius.\nget your api key\n→\n1 month free, then $19/mo\nArize summarizes patterns. Rius gives you the cause.\n\nArize groups failures on a schedule and leaves the digging to you or a chat assistant. Rius works out which step, which tool and which change caused each incident, as it happens.\n\nThen it alerts you, or your supervisor agent over MCP, with the root cause attached.\n\nsymptom\n→\npattern\n→\nroot cause\n→\nalert\nSee every end user your agents served.\n\nTraces, failures, cost and which agents touched each user, in one view. Untagged traffic is the first row, never hidden.\n\nClick a user to open their traces. Answer “did this customer have a bad experience?” in seconds.\n\nBuilt to feed your agents, not just your dashboard.\n\nRius runs as an MCP server for many agents at once. Coding agents, supervisor agents and on-call agents pull incidents, root causes and traces, so they can investigate, fix and improve themselves.\n\nThe MCP view shows which agents connect, which tools they call and whether they get an answer.\n\nincident\n→\nagent reads RCA\n→\nfix\n→\nverify\nWhat does 100k spans per month cost you?\n\nSame volume, four options. Phoenix is free to download, so set your engineer's hourly rate to see what running it costs.\n\nvolume\n100k spans / month\nengineer hourly rate (Phoenix)\n$65/h\n$10\n$100\nPhoenix infrastructure\nproduction · AWS managed\nlean · single VM\n\nRius Core\n\n$19 /mo\n\nCovers 100k spans · 500k included\ntry 1 month for free\nget started\nretention\n60d\nsetup · maintenance\n0 h\nalerts\nunlimited\nRCAs\n10/mo\nvs Phoenix: you save $324/mo\n\nPhoenix OSS\n\n$343 /mo\n\nCovers 100k spans · on your infra\n\nYear one, setup spread over 12 months.\n\nESTIMATEsetup · 11 h\n$60/mo\nESTIMATEmaint · 3 h/mo\n$195/mo\nESTIMATEinfrastructure\n$88/mo\nsetup hours\n↓\nmaintenance hours / month\n↓\ninfrastructure / month\n↓\n\nArize AX Free\n\n$0 /mo\n\nLimited to 25k spans per month\nretention\n15d\ningestion\n1 GB/mo\nSignal issues\n10/mo\n\nArize AX Pro\n\n$50 /mo\n\nLimited to 50k spans per month\nretention\n30d\ningestion\n10 GB/mo\nSignal issues\n25/mo\noverage\nprice not published\n\nPhoenix figures are estimates: AWS on-demand list prices, us-east-1; hours assume heavy AI-assisted work with Claude Code (half of a manual setup); Phoenix OSS has no built-in alerting, so building it is included.\n\nCommon questions\nWhat is the best Arize alternative for startups?\n↓\nHow much does it cost to self-host Arize Phoenix?\n↓\nDoes Arize Phoenix have real-time alerts?\n↓\nCan I run Rius and Phoenix side by side?\n↓\nPhoenix is free. Why pay $19?\n↓\nIs Phoenix open source?\n↓\nIs Rius self-hostable?\n↓\nWhat does Rius not replace?\n↓\nReady to give your agents better data and total recall?\nStart with Tares\n\nFeed your agents the right data.\n\nget_started\nStart with Rius\n\nSee and debug agents in production.\n\nget_started\nproducts\ntares\nfeed your agents the right data. open source\nrius\nsee what your agents did in production.\ncontact\ndocs\nblog\nabout\n2026 - Copyright GlassFlow.ai\nTerms & Conditions\nPrivacy Policy"